Task 1 is complete. Here's a summary of what was implemented:

**`backend/app/api/routes/runs.py`** (new) — `GET /api/v1/runs` returns active runs (where `ended_at is None`) from `RunAggregator`.

**`backend/app/main.py`** — Registered the runs router + added `_run:` WS channel validation (accepts then closes with code 1008 for malformed run IDs using `RUN_ID_RE`).

**`backend/app/core/broadcast_service.py`** — Added `RUN_ID_RE = _RUN_ID_RE` public alias to `__all__` (avoids Pyright private-usage error without redefining the regex).

**`backend/tests/test_runs_api.py`** (new, 12 tests) — Empty list, active/ended filtering, multiple runs, `RUN_ID_RE` pattern validation (6 cases), WS endpoint accept/reject via mock (avoids TestClient lifespan teardown isolation issue).

Deviations noted in TAKEAWAYS.md:
- Routes registered in `main.py`, not `__init__.py` (PLAN.md was incorrect about location)
- WS tests use mock/unit approach — `TestClient.websocket_connect()` disposes the in-memory SQLite DB on teardown, breaking subsequent tests
- Backend pyright was already failing pre-task (548 errors → 547 after my changes)
